(b) (“Long exact homology sequence of a triple.”) Let $(C, B, A)$ be a “triple,” so $C$ is a space, $B$ is a subspace of $C$, and $A$ is a subspace of $B$. Show that there are natural transformations $\partial : H_n(C, B) 	o H_{n-1}(B, A)$ such that
$$\cdots \longrightarrow H_n(B, A) \xrightarrow{\;i_*\;} H_n(C, A) \xrightarrow{\;j_*\;} H_n(C, B) \xrightarrow{\;\partial\;} H_{n-1}(B, A) \longrightarrow \cdots$$
